 ## Background
-Neural Textures Architecture extends the concept of traditional 2D texture mapping into the neural rendering domain. It was introduced as part of the broader exploration of explicit representations in neural rendering, offering a hybrid approach between explicit mesh-based rendering and implicit neural fields [S1]. The method leverages differentiable rasterization to bridge the gap between standard graphics pipelines and neural optimization [S1].
